  "title": "Newborn Umbilical Cord Care: A Pediatrician's Guide for New Parents",
  "summary": "Newborn umbilical cord care is simpler than most parents expect. Keep the stump clean and dry — no alcohol or creams needed. It usually falls off within 1 to 2 weeks (up to 3 is normal). Learn normal vs. warning signs, safe bathing, and when to call your pediatrician.",
